WEBVTT

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:50.630
During mid june, the Queen's Class is
preparing for the upcoming examinations.

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.630
A final mock exam is held.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.580
The mock exam is in the same
format as the upcoming exam.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.780
Geometry, Algebra, Latin and English.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.380
All these subjects are covered over three days.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.190
During this time, Anne is so
nervous that she cannot eat.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.230
And so, the day when the
results will be announced arrives.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.580
Well then, I will give you your
report cards of the mock exam,

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.630
and the admission cards that
arrived from Queen's Academy.

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:35.700
I will not announce the results,
but everyone did very well.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.470
If you keep this up,
I'm sure everyone will make it.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:44.460
After today, Queen's Class will be disbanded.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.210
There's one final thing I want you to promise me.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.560
That is not to touch your textbooks
before the exam.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.030
You are all very well-prepared.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.950
If you try to study all night before the exam,

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.780
it will only make you tired and
will cause you to make mistakes.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:06.790
Don't think about the exam.
Take walks and go to bed early at night.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.250
I will accompany you to the exam.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.110
Now then, when I call your
name, please come to me.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.510
Josie Pye.
- Here

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:17.840
Anne Shirley.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:19.980
Here you are, Josie.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.250
Here you are, Anne.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.240
Moody McPherson.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.530
Charlie Sloan.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.230
How did you do, Anne?

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:28.320
All right, I guess.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.090
Ruby Gillis.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:30.040
Here.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.210
Jane Andrews.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.320
Gilbert Blythe.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.200
Number 13!

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.470
It's not a very good number.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.390
What number is it?

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:47.640
Number 13.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.270
Anne, 13 is a very unlucky number.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:55.080
Oh? Why is it unlucky?

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:56.650
Don't you know?

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:00.370
The number 13 has been called unlucky for ages.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:04.330
I know that, but it's merely superstition.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.850
It doesn't matter to me.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:08.890
Really? If it was me, I would worry.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.170
Ahhh! I'm so glad it wasn't me!

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.810
English, 98 marks.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.800
N-number 13?

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:25.060
Josie said that it's a very unlucky number.
But that's just common superstition, right?!

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:28.550
W-well now... of course... yes...

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.820
It's silly superstition, Anne.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.490
After all, you've got such a good
grade in the first place.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.580
This is nothing to panic about.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.630
T-that's right, Anne.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:42.030
I want to think so, too, but I
wish I got a different number after all.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.400
I'll probably lie awake all through the night,
thinking: What if I don't make it?

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:51.390
Then you'll go to school for another
year, and re-take it next year.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.230
Oh, I don't believe I'd have the heart for it. It would be such a disgrace to fail.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.780
Especially if Gil... if the others passed.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:04.410
Somehow, I have a feeling that something
outrageous will happen because of this number.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:08.280
Really, I never thought you would
be this superstitious.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.510
Don't worry, Anne.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:16.730
It doesn't matter if your admission number is 13 or 0.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.280
I'm sure you will beat the other students
from this island and become number one.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:24.800
That isn't possible, Matthew.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:30.090
No, that's what I've always believed.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:37.350
It's the end of June, and the final
day of the semester has come.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.880
This day is the last day of
Miss Stacy's tenure as a teacher.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.480
Three years have gone by in a flash,

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:49.940
but I remember every moment
I shared with all of you,

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.830
and I will remember all of your faces.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:59.780
I have written a letter, filled
with memories, for each of you.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.110
Miss Stacy's farewell speech is quite fuss-free

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:06.850
compared with that of Mr. Phillips' three years ago.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.910
However, the students' hankies
are already soaked.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:14.690
This shows how attached
the students are to her.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:21.760
Tommy, read this later. You must
continue with your insect research.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:22.630
Yes.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:23.870
Take care.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.350
Yes. You take care, too.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.270
Next one is Diana Barry.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.500
Yes.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.780
Diana, I will never forget your
very sweet voice.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.190
Miss Stacy...

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:44.580
Goodbye.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:45.980
Miss Stacy!

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.550
It does seem as if it was the end of everything.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:17.820
But, Diana, you oughtn't to feel half as badly as I do.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.030
You can come back here again
at the beginning of next semester.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:27.780
But I don't even know if I will get
to call it my Alma Mater.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.230
It all depends on my luck.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.930
It won't be a bit the same.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:36.240
Miss Stacy won't be here anymore.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:39.470
And you, Jane, and Ruby
won't be here anymore, right?

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.880
I shall have to sit all alone,

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.290
for I couldn't bear to have another deskmate after you.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.350
Oh, we have had jolly times, haven't we, Anne?

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.670
It's dreadful to think they're all over.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:01.900
If you would stop crying, I could.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:07.940
Just as soon as I put away my hanky, I see you
brimming up and that starts me off again.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.520
You are making me cry as well.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.770
Maybe I'll be coming here for
the new semester, after all.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:21.210
I have a feeling I won't pass the exam.
I've started having this feeling more often.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:25.520
But Anne, you did very well in
the mock exam Miss Stacy gave, right?

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:26.360
Yes.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:29.760
But those exams didn't make me nervous.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:31.790
When I think of the real exam,

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:35.170
you can't imagine what a horrid, cold,
fluttery feeling comes round my heart.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.190
And then my number is thirteen!

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.970
That's nothing to worry about.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:42.930
I do wish I was going in with you.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:46.240
Moreover, I wish we could have
a splendid time together in town.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.040
But that's impossible, isn't it?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.860
I suppose you'll have to cram
in the evenings, won't you?

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:57.620
No. Miss Stacy has made us promise
not to open a book at all.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:02.300
She told us not to think about the
exam and to go to bed early at night.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:05.760
It's good advice, but I expect
it will be hard to follow.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.110
Good advice is apt to be, I think.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:11.660
Prissy Andrews told me that she sat up half
the night every night of her Entrance week

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.240
and crammed for dear life.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:17.810
So I have determined to sit
up AT LEAST as long as she did.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:24.270
It was so kind of your Aunt Josephine to
ask me to stay at Beechwood during the exam.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.490
Anne, you'll write to me while
you're in town, won't you?

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.860
Of course. I'll write Tuesday night and
tell you how the first day goes.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.920
Then I'll be haunting the post office on Wednesday.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:35.960
It's a promise.

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:36.960
Yes. I promise.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:44.630
Matthew is looking forward to driving Anne to
Charlottetown in the horse-drawn carriage himself,

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:49.410
but on the night before the departure,
Matthew has a heart attack.

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:52.410
Although Matthew keeps insisting
that he is all right,

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.080
Marilla wants to be careful and
decides to have Anne go by train instead.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.380
I'm all packed.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:05.380
Anne, there's something wrong with
one of the cows, and Matthew can't leave.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:08.050
I will take you to Carmody in
the horse-drawn carriage.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.120
It's unfortunate, but you
will have to take the train.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.570
I see. I understand!

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.810
I'm sorry, Anne. On this
long-awaited important day...

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.290
Oh, don't worry about it, Matthew!
I'm just a little disappointed.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.100
I'm off!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.690
Do your best!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:06.540
It's been a long time since I took a ride
in a horse-drawn carriage with you.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.820
Yes.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:11.720
It was four years ago. The day after
you came to Green Gables.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:15.160
I took you to the home of Mr. Spencer's wife.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.890
Somehow, it seems like a dream now, Marilla.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.240
I'm recalling a lot
from the past today.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.370
Oh yes, Matthew didn't
look too good earlier.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.030
Really, he's just getting old.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:34.040
And not being able to
take you saddens him.

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:36.330
He had been intent on doing it.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:37.780
I understand.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.930
Even if I can't live up to Matthew's
expectations of being first,

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.990
I'll try my best to be on the Top 10 list for sure.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:49.430
You don't need to get that worked up.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:51.230
I told you the other day,

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:52.420
that even if you fail,

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:55.940
you can go to school for another year
and wait for the next opportunity.

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:00.960
But I'm not worried about it at all.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.850
You should try to feel the same way.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.780
Marilla...

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:53.240
Anne!

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.870
I'm sorry for having made
you come to pick me up.

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.160
It's nothing. Now, come this way.

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:06.860
I was surprised when I read your sudden telegram,

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:09.420
but I'm just glad you didn't get lost.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:12.870
The cows are sick again. That's why
Matthew's not here with me.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.120
I see. He must be very worried about them, right?

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:18.870
Since we're so close, why don't
we go by Queen's Academy?

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:19.980
Oh my!

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.890
Look, right over there.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:47.680
What do you think, Anne?

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.530
You will be studying here in September.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:53.550
It's even grander than I thought, Miss Barry.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:56.610
I will send you here every day
during your exams.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:01.560
Well... Miss Stacy is supposed to
accompany us for those three days...

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.970
Really now?! Well, then let me accompany
you to the entrance ceremony.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:11.990
Yes, of course you can do that!
But I don't even know if I will manage to pass.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:16.130
No. As far as I'm concerned, you'll definitely pass.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:28.170
My goodness!

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.860
A little while ago you said you mightn't pass,

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:33.400
and now you say you want
to be in the Top 10 list?

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:34.560
Yes.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.560
That will not be easy.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:42.690
And I heard that there is a boy
that is your rival. Is that so?

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.930
Yes. I don't want to lose to him,

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:48.670
but I really want to get good
grades for Marilla and Matthew.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:51.030
Especially for Matthew.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:56.540
After all, Matthew believes I'm
going to become number one.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:57.980
That's strange, isn't it?

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:00.380
No, that's not strange at all.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:04.630
No matter how ambitious I am,
I can't reach that position.

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:10.190
But if I were to be among the top 10,
they would both be very happy, right?

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:12.960
I want to see that
look on their faces.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:19.030
I envy those two.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:27.430
On Monday morning, Miss Stacy

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.730
picks up all the female
students at the boarding house

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:32.000
in a horse-drawn carriage as she has planned.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:35.390
Good morning.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.640
Anne, feel my hand.

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:49.870
It's cold as ice, Ruby.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.500
But, Anne, you look rather pale, too.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.030
You stayed up all night studying, didn't you?

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.260
Me?! Of course not!

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.930
Even if you did that, and pass the exam,

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:03.370
I don't believe you're strong enough to
stand the grind of the teacher's course.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:06.570
Josie, everyone's nervous today.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.690
Now, let's forget all about it.
Take a deep breath.

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:11.580
1, 2, 3.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:16.680
One more time.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:34.690
8x4=32, 8x5=40...

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:38.510
- There's Moody Spurgeon.
- ...8x9=72...

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.920
Good morning.

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:41.480
What are you doing here?

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:43.480
I think he's memorising his
multiplication table.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.690
Be quiet! Don't disturb me!

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.160
If I don't do this, I will get upset

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.520
and will forget everything I ever learned.

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:56.130
But once I recite my table, I can
keep the facts in their proper place.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:57.900
That's impossible!

00:16:58.020 --> 00:16:59.050
It's true!

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:03.900
Ah! Now look, because of you, everything
is spinning around inside my head!

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:07.150
2x2=4, 2x3=6, 2x4=8, 2x5=10...

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:09.080
Good morning.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:12.010
Looks like everyone's here.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:14.880
Oh, Moody, are you feeling ill?

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.390
No, I'm all right.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:20.820
All of you have the ability to make it,
so you should calm yourselves.

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:21.720
Okay!

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:25.340
Well then, let's do some gymnastics
before we enter the class room.

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:46.550
Uh, the English exam will now begin.

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:50.040
You're not allowed to look around or talk.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.240
Well, I will be handing out the paper now.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.270
The English exam is in the morning,

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:01.000
and after lunch, they will have the History test.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.360
Oh Moody, you were very quick.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:10.360
Anne, what am I going to do?

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:13.710
It's over for me. I'm sure
I'll fail the History test.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:18.160
I think it was difficult, too.
I mixed up some dates.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:21.080
I'm taking the train home tomorrow, Anne.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:25.410
I feel as if I was born to
disappoint my parents.

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.850
It's impossible for me to become a pastor anyway.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.790
That's no good, Moody!
You have to complete the exam.

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:34.090
That would be bad to
Miss Stacy, don't you think?

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.800
What's wrong with Ruby?

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:47.800
Anne, I heard that she made an
unbelievable mistake in the English test.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:51.370
I just told her what the answer was.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:54.680
What on earth is going on?

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:57.050
Miss Stacy, I... I...

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:02.260
Ruby, it's common to make mistakes.

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:05.850
Don't brood over it.
Just try harder tomorrow.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.120
Hey, let's all do something to
raise our spirits tomorrow.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.710
Let's go get Gilbert and Jane.

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:18.740
Diana, Miss Stacy treated us all to ice cream.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:22.580
Everyone reacted like children all at once.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:26.640
Everyone said that it would be
so good if you were there, too.

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.790
It's Tuesday evening now.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:32.280
I'm writing this letter in the reading
room of Beechwood house.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.790
The geometry exam is tomorrow.

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:39.240
Thinking about it, I recall my
promise to Miss Stacy,

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:43.320
trying not to open those books.
It takes a lot of determination.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:50.570
If repeating tables were useful, I would
be reciting them until morning.

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:54.270
Oh, Diana, I wish the Geometry test was over already.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.640
But just as Mrs. Lynde said,

00:19:56.910 --> 00:20:02.450
no matter if I pass or fail Geometry,
the sun will fall and rise like always.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:05.020
That's right,

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:08.520
but if I fail, I almost wish
the sun will stop shining.

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:10.980
Oh, Anne!

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:13.760
Oh, I wonder if she is taking geometry about now.

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.100
It'll be fine.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:39.930
You were confident about all
the other subjects, weren't you?

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:42.110
It's only your geometry, right?

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.430
Hey, Charlie!

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:46.750
How did you do in geometry?

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.780
I think it was all right.
Question 4 wasn't easy though.

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:53.860
Oh, that one. It's actually pretty easy if you
keep your eye on the rotational movement.

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:56.210
It's Triangle DBA plus Triangle EAC.

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.770
- Anne, I'll go there just for a bit.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:58.220
It's Triangle DBA plus Triangle EAC.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.900
When you do that, it becomes a triangle, right?

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.620
My letter is three pages long!

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.590
Oh... Three pages...

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:18.380
She wrote this much in order
to overcome the temptation

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.700
to open the geometry book yesterday evening!

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.700
It's very good. Listen to this:

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:26.340
"Diana, when I first
got the exam paper,"

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:29.400
"my hands grew cold and I felt dizzy."

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.500
"It was only for a moment,
but it was very scary."

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:35.340
"I felt the same way
I did four years ago,"

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:39.980
"when I asked Marilla if I could
stay at Green Gables."

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.580
"But my mind cleared up."

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:46.190
"My heart returned to normal."

00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:50.970
"I almost forgot to mention that
it had stopped completely till then." she says!

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:57.490
The examinations in the three
subjects are over by Thursday.

00:21:57.760 --> 00:22:02.630
The examinees say a true goodbye
to Miss Stacy this time.

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:05.390
They thank her from the
bottom of their hearts.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:15.350
And on Friday, Anne says
goodbye to Miss Josephine Barry

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:18.550
and returns by train, just as she had
when she had come from Carmody.

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:22.770
In Carmody, Matthew is waiting for her.

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:28.630
Diana is waiting for the two
to arrive at Green Gables.

00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:30.860
Anne! Welcome back!

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:32.940
Diana! I'm home!

00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:37.150
You look quite cheerful, Anne!

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:40.860
Since you went to town,
I've been waiting for this day.

00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:42.930
Welcome home, Anne.

00:22:43.450 --> 00:22:44.650
Marilla, I'm home.

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:47.270
I'm so glad to be back home!

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.150
There's no place in the world
better than Green Gables.

00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:52.250
Anne, how did the tests go?

00:22:52.550 --> 00:22:56.090
Except for geometry, I think
I did well on everything.

00:22:56.510 --> 00:22:58.910
I don't know if I passed geometry.

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:01.980
I have a bad feeling I didn't do well.

00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:03.800
That's impossible!

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:05.390
How did the others do?

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:10.530
The girls say they know they didn't pass, but I think they did pretty well.

00:23:11.040 --> 00:23:15.860
Josie says the geometry was so easy a child of ten could do it!

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:19.150
But the truth is that no one knows!

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:21.650
It's impossible to know until
the announcement has been made,

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:23.740
and that's in two weeks time!

00:23:23.930 --> 00:23:26.790
Anne, how did Gilbert do?

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:28.390
Gil?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:32.730
He should have done well.
He looked very confident.

00:23:33.230 --> 00:23:36.200
Oh, it'll be all right. I'm sure you'll pass.

00:23:36.630 --> 00:23:40.460
But if the results aren't good,
I'd rather not pass at all.

00:23:40.570 --> 00:23:43.570
Well, well. You're quite competitive, aren't you?

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:46.740
Oh, that isn't true. Right, Matthew?

00:23:47.050 --> 00:23:48.830
Well, that's true...

00:23:49.190 --> 00:23:51.840
Well, at any rate, we
will eat delicious food tonight

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:53.960
and then you must have a good rest, Anne.

00:23:54.420 --> 00:23:55.070
Diana.

00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:59.340
You and Anne must have a lot to talk about.
Please stay for dinner.

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:02.170
Please do, Diana!

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:02.950
Yes.

00:24:05.220 --> 00:24:09.930
After that, Anne waits for the announcement
which will be made after two weeks.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:20.330
Two weeks pass after the end of the test.

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:24.340
And even after three weeks, no announcement
of the results has been made.

00:24:24.580 --> 00:24:27.340
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 39

00:24:27.630 --> 00:24:28.810
The Announcement of the Results

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:30.450
Please look forward to it!
